{
  "description": "Front Garden:  T1-T2 & T3: 3 x Birches: Approximately 10.00m-13.00m: Reduce back to previous and most recent points of reduction (approximately 2.20m) whilst retaining approximately 30% of shortened furnishing growth. Remove dead wood throughout the crown. Remove epicormic growth from the low stem.\rT4: Birch: Approximately 9.00m: This tree has been slightly suppressed by neighbouring trees. It leans back towards the building. Reduce back to previous and most recent points of reduction, up to approximately 1.50m. Remove dead wood. Thin crown density by 10%-15%.\r\r\rT5: Birch: Approximately 13.00m: Reduce crown by approximately 1.20m-1.50m, reducing back to previous points of reduction. Thin crown density by approximately 20%. Remove major deadwood throughout the crown.\r\rRear Garden:\r\rT6: Mature Ash: Approximately 11.00m: Reduce crown by approximately 1.50m-2.00m, not below previous reduction points whilst preserving fine furnishing growth, to maintain a natural crown profile.\rThin crown density by 20%-25%, removing weak epicormic growth and dead wood throughout.\r\rG1: Mixed species tree/hedge line: Approximately 8.00m: Consisting of: Evergreen Oak, Magnolia Grandiflora, Hawthorn, Bay, Mulberry, Fig & Olives:\rThe Bay trees within the group have started to outgrow neighbouring trees. Reduce over extended branches of the Bays by up to 2.20m back into the main group height line. Tip prune smaller tree to maintain a continued compact but naturally undulating hedge height line, up to 1.50m.\rTrim evergreen Oak at the end of the arc to tidy. Reduce lateral and sub lateral growth, encroaching over the lawn and towards the house, by up to approximately 1.50m as necessary, to control encroachment.\r\rControl encroachment/general maintnenace.",
